 "final_message": "All eleven work items are done, and the test suite passes (6 tests).\n\n- **`metrics.py`:**\n  - `conversion_rate` returns `0.0` for an empty list and counts only `True` as converted.\n  - `pooled_conversion_rate` divides total converted sessions by total sessions, and returns `0.0` when there are none.\n  - `conversions_in_window` sums the last `days` entries. It returns `0` when `days` is 0 and sums the whole list when `days` is longer than it.\n- **`loader.py`:**\n  - `parse_session_log` skips blank lines, whitespace-only lines and `#` comment lines. It trims whitespace around each field and reads `converted` as `1`, `0` or empty (None).\n  - `dedupe_sessions` keeps the last session for each id, sorted by day and then id.\n  - `daily_conversion_counts` returns one entry per day from start to end inclusive. Days with no conversions get `0`, sessions outside the range are ignored, and an end before the start gives an empty list.\n- **`report.py`:** `campaign_summary` rounds `rate` to 3 decimals and counts only groups that contain at least one session.\n- **Tests:** I added one test for `None` counting as not converted, and one for the last duplicate id being kept.\n- **README:** I corrected the `conversions_in_window` entry and added one for `daily_conversion_counts`.\n\nSPEC doesn't say what a negative `days` should do in `conversions_in_window`. I made it return `0`, the same as `days == 0`.\n\nI didn't add tests for the other sections.",
